  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: One more day of lower RH then moisture and storm\nchances increase Wednesday into the weekend.\n\nArea of high pressure from the Great Lakes to western VA will\nprovide fall like cooler temperatures this morning then with\ndry airmass and sunshine warm us up to near seasonal levels\ntoday. \n\nWednesday, the surface high shifts east, allowing for some\nreturn moisture to creep up the southern Appalachians. A\nshortwave arrives by Wednesday evening, and anticipate some\nwidely scattered showers/storms to form mid afternoon especially\nalong the Blue Ridge from Boone to Roanoke. Curtailed PoPs\ncompared to the NBM, as it was showing more coverage, and return\nmoisture should be a little delayed.\n\nA front approaches later Thursday and the upper trough will be\nalong/west of the Appalachians with southwest flow and \nincreasing lift. Several shortwaves move across Thursday into \nFriday, so increasing chances for showers/storms for much of the\narea. Will have to watch for storms to train/repeat over same \nlocations as front slows down. \n\nThe upper trough should nudge east by the weekend with lower\nchances for showers/storms, while 5h heights increase going into\nearly next week returning the heat.",
